    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.21_ologs_and_typed_english.chapters.01_olog_as_typed_english.sections.02_four_artifacts_of_olog.concrete_anchor_1_Boxes#domesticcatbox" .
silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_01_olog_as_typed_english_sections_02_four_artifacts_of_olog_concrete_anchor_1_Boxes#domesticcatbox silm:hasLongDescription "The DomesticCatBox is the boxes set: typed-noun objects of O_eng; e.g. a domestic cat, a body mass quality. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Boxes', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
